WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.917
Here's Al-Duha, and right below it on the same page, Al-Sharh begins.

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:32.055
Let's select the last ayah of Al-Duha, “talk about the blessings of
your Lord,” and the first of Al-Sharh, “Did We not relieve your
heart for you?”, and ask why this surah comes right after Al-Duha.

00:00:32.055 --> 00:00:37.555
The answer reads the two surahs as one conversation,
and goes to the exact point where they meet.

00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:42.355
Al-Duha: speak of My blessings. Al-Sharh: remember the blessings I gave you.

00:00:42.355 --> 00:00:55.055
Al-Biqāʿī's Naẓm al-Durar says so explicitly, and Ibn ʿĀshūr traces three
connections: past care, future reassurance, and a response to blessings.
